{# The existing split and figure compose the page's opening claim. Its picture
   is the one that does not open at full size. It stands beside the claim as
   decoration, and there is nothing in it to read closer.

   The two are level and not top-aligned. Decoration that hangs from the
   first line of a claim reads as a column that ran out of words.

   Neither half is a stack. The claim is a flow of blocks that carry their own
   step. The picture is one thing — a container that spaces a single child
   spaces nothing. #}
<div class="sds-sections">
    <div class="sds-split sds-split--center">
        <div class="sds-column">
            {{- renderNode(node.children|first) -}}
        </div>
        <div class="sds-column">
            <sds-figure src="{{ asset(node.option('src')) }}" alt="{{ node.option('alt') }}"></sds-figure>
        </div>
    </div>
    {%- for child in node.children|slice(1) -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</div>
